---
import ContentLayout from '../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const noSlash = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const u = (p: string) => `${noSlash}${p}`;
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Software Support and Maintenance, Including Apps We Didn't Build | Freedom45"
  description="Freedom45 supports and maintains web and mobile apps after launch, including software built by someone else: fixes, security updates, monitoring, performance and new features."
  activePage="services"
>
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">Support and maintenance</p>
    <h1>Launched isn't <span class="g">finished.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">Software needs looking after: fixes, security updates, the odd emergency and the next round of features. We do that for what we build, and we'll happily take on software we didn't.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>Taking over software someone else built</h2>
    <p>Maybe the original developer has moved on, the agency has gone quiet, or nobody's quite sure how it works any more. We start with an honest review of the code: what's sound, what's risky and what to fix first, in plain English. Then we take it on.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What's included</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><h3>Fixes and updates</h3><p>Bugs fixed, and security and dependency updates kept current.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Monitoring</h3><p>We keep an eye on it, so problems are spotted early.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Performance</h3><p>Making a slow or creaking system fast and stable again.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>The next features</h3><p>Steady improvements, planned around what your users need.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Yours, whoever looks after it</h2>
    <p>The code, data and accounts stay yours, documented so anyone can pick them up. Hosted by us or on your own hosting. You're never locked in.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where to next</h2>
    <p class="related">
      <a href={u('/services/web-and-mobile-apps')}>Web and mobile apps</a>
      <a href={u('/how-we-work')}>How we work</a>
      <a href={u('/commitments')}>Our commitments</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>
